# ============================================================================
# 06_ Build ASPC and fibroblast-stroma signatures — v8 SCORE RANKING
# ============================================================================
#
# SELECTION RULE
#   1. Build branch-specific candidate pools from 03_ marker recurrence.
#   2. Keep candidate genes measured in the supplied bulk expression matrix.
#   3. Calculate the existing weighted evidence_score for each candidate.
#   4. Sort by evidence_score DESCENDING, then gene symbol ASCENDING for ties.
#   5. Select up to cfg$target_size genes per branch.
#
# IMPORTANT CHANGES FROM v7
#   - No adaptive threshold ladder.
#   - No hard tau, target-ratio, NEPC/AR-correlation, or score gates.
#   - No named-gene rescue or forced inclusion.
#   - AR may enter the ASPC candidate pool but competes on evidence_score.
#   - Fibroblast-first exclusion is retained as an explicit configurable policy.
#   - Ranked files include explicit rank and selection information.
#
# WHAT IS RETAINED
#   - Existing evidence and annotation weights.
#   - Branch-specific tau and atlas support.
#   - Imported elastic-net, stability, and WGCNA flags.
#   - CSPA surface annotations, cache, and explicit fallback.
#   - TNFSF12 and MDK ligand annotation overrides.
#   - Unweighted mean gene-wise z-score for bulk signature scoring.
#
# INTERPRETATION
#   - evidence_score is a manually weighted prioritization score.
#   - Annotation membership is not proof of ASPC identity.
#   - Selection does not require cross-cohort replication beyond the configured
#     candidate-pool recurrence requirement.
#   - Selection does not guarantee NEPC-positive or AR-negative correlation.
#   - Missing evidence contributes zero points, not proof of biological absence.
#   - Zero-score genes may be selected if needed to fill the requested size.
#   - The input bulk values are used as supplied. No library-size normalization
#     or log transformation is introduced by this script.
#
# IMPLEMENTATION NOTE
#   Partial correlations are calculated using base-R QR residualization of BOTH
#   gene expression and ASPC_fraction against the same usable covariates.
#   They are unavailable if the fraction/covariates or residual variation are
#   insufficient. They are not converted into hard selection gates.
# ============================================================================

